        "window_seconds": 1,
        "budget_points": 2,
        "read_cost": 1,
        "write_cost": 10
    },
    "widget_ref": "ui://core/daily-report",
    "_ai_53_notes": {
        "quota": "AI-53 A CONFIRMER EN STORY: Shopify applique des call limits PAR PLAN MARCHAND (leaky bucket REST: 2 req/s standard, 4 req/s Shopify Plus, bucket 40/80). review-15-4 F-3: l'engine core est un FIXED-WINDOW (recharge complete par fenetre) et ne modelise PAS le leaky bucket -- une fenetre 60s/40pts autoriserait un BURST de 40 requetes instantanees (plus permissif que Shopify, pas 'prudent'). Profil retenu: window 1s / 2 points = 2 req/s soutenu SANS burst (approximation conservatrice du bucket standard). Le vrai backstop reste le handler 429 -> RateLimitError. A recalibrer via X-Shopify-Shop-Api-Call-Limit en passe live (Phase B).",
        "canonical_metric_mapping": "AI-53 A CONFIRMER EN STORY: noms de champs API Admin REST supposes d'apres la doc: order.total_price -> revenue (montant total commande, additif), order.total_refunded (ou somme des refund.transactions) -> refund_amount (COLONNE DEDIEE, JAMAIS soustrait silencieusement de revenue), comptage d'ordres -> orders_count. A verifier endpoint/champs exacts (Admin REST vs GraphQL) en passe live (AI-53/AI-13).",
        "transaction_id": "AI-53 A CONFIRMER EN STORY: transaction_id expose comme DIMENSION DE DETAIL du raw (une commande -> une/plusieurs transactions de paiement Shopify). C'est la cle de jointure GA4 x Shopify (Epic 17). Le mart agrege au JOUR: transaction_id N'est PAS une partition de breakdown du mart. Disponibilite exacte (order.transactions[].id vs order.id) a confirmer via la doc Admin API.",
        "refunds_decision": "DECISION 15.4 (REFERENCE pour Stripe 15.7): les remboursements sont stockes en COLONNE DEDIEE refund_amount (metrique additive positive), JAMAIS soustraits silencieusement de revenue. Le net se calcule au niveau semantique (revenue - refund_amount) de facon explicite et auditable."
    },
    "_error_map_note": "Shopify Admin REST uses pure HTTP status semantics: 401=Unauthorized (expired/invalid token), 402=Payment Required (shop suspended), 403=Forbidden (permission scope missing), 423=Locked (shop locked), 429=Too Many Requests (leaky-bucket overflow, handled by RateLimitError path). No provider-level numeric error codes refine beyond the HTTP status; error_map is intentionally empty. The 429 path keeps raising core.quota.RateLimitError directly (Story 3.3 breaker contract). All other non-200 responses raise via classify_http_error(status_code, body) with an empty map, relying on pure-HTTP classification.",
    "error_map": {},
    "_account_topology_note": "Shopify is shop-scoped: one OAuth token = one merchant store. There is no account hierarchy to discover or select; the shop_domain is the sole scope and is resolved from the connection's Nango credential at pull time. account_topology is therefore absent from this manifest by design, not by omission.",
